d businesses build, manage, and deploy agentic AI applications on infrastructure. Its direct applications and integrations include Claude Code, a coding agent that handles multi-step software development tasks; Claude Cowork, a work agent that has computer-use capability and enables it to work with professionals on end-to-end business tasks; Claude.ai, a conversational product for enterprises, teams, and individuals; Claude Security, a defensive cybersecurity product; Claude Duet, a proactive agent that monitors connected applications, provide daily briefings, perform tasks, and builds web applications while operating on a cloud-based virtual machine; Claude Tag, a collaborative agent that works alongside teams in productivity tools; Claude Design, which enables users to create polished designs, prototypes, presentations, and other visual work through natural language conversation and direct editing; and Claude Science, an AI workbench for scientific research that brings literature analysis, data processing, and manuscript preparation into a single desktop environment. The company serves financial services, healthcare, life sciences, law, and education industries. Anthropic, PBC was incorporated in 2021 and is based in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Dario  Amodei | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 42 | Compensation: $4.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $865K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers. Stock-based compensation of $218K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). R&D investment of 138% of revenue (heavy) signals commitment to product development and talent.","financial_summary":["Anthropic, PBC is a mega-cap technology business with a $1.2T market cap on $4.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +957% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence t